<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tunku Abdul Rahman</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1903–1990</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tunku Abdul Rahman was a prince of the Kedah royal family who led the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-malays-national-organisation">United Malays National Organisation</a> from 1951. He negotiated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malaya">Malaya</a>'s independence from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a>, proclaiming it in 1957, and became the first prime minister of the Federation of Malaya. He then led the formation of Malaysia in 1963 and remained prime minister until 1970.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tunku-abdul-rahman.jpg" alt="Tunku Abdul Rahman" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tunku_abd_rahman_(cropped,_4to3_port,_bypass).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
